(The control for bug #55: when the `treating` clause's match agrees with
 the element type of the collection being walked, the substitution still
 fires - over a list literal, over a named list, and over numbers as well
 as text. Rejecting the mismatch must not narrow any of these.)

a list called sources is ["-", "report.txt"].
print each source from ["-", "report.txt"] treating "-" as "/dev/stdin".
print each source from sources treating "-" as "/dev/stdin".
print each score from [1, 2] treating 1 as 9.
print each step from 1 to 3 treating 2 as 20.
